 ## Overview
-The Dodecahedron Modulo method computes the signed distance from a point to the surface of a regular dodecahedron by folding the input space into a fundamental region using a sequence of reflections and rotations, then returning the folded point [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the shared computational framework of [Basic Primitive Definitions](5346-basic-primitive-definitions.md) and belongs to the [Polyhedral Primitives](2529-polyhedral-primitives.md) family, alongside primitives like the [Octahedron Signed Distance Function](2339-octahedron-signed-distance-function.md) and [Hexagonal Prism Signed Distance Function](2348-hexagonal-prism-signed-distance-function.md).
